pp":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pola-rs/polars/issues/comments/1182507291","html_url":"https://github.com/pola-rs/polars/issues/3877#issuecomment-1182507291","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pola-rs/polars/issues/3877","id":1182507291,"node_id":"IC_kwDOD7gq785Ge6Eb","user":{"login":"universalmind303","id":21327470,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzI3NDcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21327470?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303","html_url":"https://github.com/universalmind303","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-12T21:14:57Z","updated_at":"2022-07-12T21:16:27Z","body":"@ritchie46, some more discovery shows this isn't limited to serde. You can't use `LazyFrame::from` at all without manually setting the `file_cache` state. \r\n\r\nI would expect `LazyFrame::from` to return a collectable Lazyframe if I have a valid LogicalPlan. It shouldn't be able produce a lazyframe that can not be collected.\r\n\r\nThe lazyframe *should* know how to properly construct itself from a LogicalPlan, otherwise this should be a fallible operation. \r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n```rust\r\nlet lf = LazyCsvReader::new(path).finish();\r\nlet lp = lf.logical_plan;\r\nlet lf_from_lp = LazyFrame::from(lp);\r\n\r\n// panicked at 'called `Option::unwrap()  /polars/polars-lazy/src/physical_plan/file_cache.rs:43:55\r\nlet df = lf_from_lp.collect()?; \r\n```","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pola-rs/polars/issues/comments/1182507291/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"universalmind303","id":21327470,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzI3NDcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21327470?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303","html_url":"https://github.com/universalmind303","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/universalmind303/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":6981135392,"node_id":"MEE_lADOD7gq785NCuTEzwAAAAGgG6wg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pola-rs/polars/issues/events/6981135392","actor":{"login":"ritchie46","id":3023000,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMjMwMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3023000?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ritchie46","html_url":"https://github.com/ritchie46","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ritchie46/fo